From a3ae2894a2e78af51288a55acb2ee6aed7a7f177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:22:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] testsuite: microblaze: run tests for integer compare and
 branch

gcc.target/microblaze has no test that runs the integer compare and
branch patterns.  Add three, each checking every signed and unsigned
comparison, register against register and against constants, both as a
branch and as a value, on operands at the sign and carry boundaries:

- cmp-branch-run.c for int, through branch_compare (cmp and cmpu into
  r18) and branch_zero.
- cmp-branch-di-run.c for long long.
- cmp-branch-pcmp-run.c with -mxl-pattern-compare, which also scans for
  the pcmpeq and pcmpne that seq_internal_pat and sne_internal_pat emit.

The expected results come from a table computed on the host.  All three
pass on microblaze-elf and microblazeel-elf under QEMU.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/cmp-branch-run.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/cmp-branch-di-run.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/microblaze/others/cmp-branch-pcmp-run.c: New test.
